  "fullPassage": "Online shopping has been much more popular in recent years. It is expected to continue to grow, given how digitalization and the internet allow companies to sell without a physical presence. Factors such as convenience, a wider selection of goods, and lower prices have contributed to the increase in online shopping. Let's explore the biggest online shopping trends and see where things are headed.\nFirst, more people will shop through social commerce. Social media and SNS services have become increasingly popular places for consumers to discover, research, and purchase products. Social commerce makes shopping a more convenient and interactive experience, which helps explain why it's become so popular. Features like \"buy\" buttons and instant messaging tools make social media easy to use. In 2021, around 96.9 million US shoppers made a purchase through social media. Looking ahead, this trend is unlikely to slow down. In the US, social commerce earnings are estimated to reach nearly $80 billion by 2025. Plus, by 2025, the number of social commerce buyers in the United States is forecasted to reach over 114 million.\nSecond, more shoppers will use voice searches. Voice assistants were once used only to get directions, to answer questions about weather, or to call someone. But the way people use voice searches is changing. Voice assistants are now becoming a core component of online shopping. In 2022, as much as $40 billion of sales used a voice search. This represents a significant leap compared to the $2 billion worth of sales in 2017. It appears shoppers are only going to increase their use of voice searches.",
